{
 "name": "Pinwheel House",
 "notes": "A 40 by 40 metre house and garden. Four wings turn around the skylit 12 metre playroom like a pinwheel, so every wing has a door to the playroom, to both neighbouring wings and out to the garden loop. The loop runs round the house through the garden, patio, pool lawn with its paddling pool, side yard and the shed in the north-west corner. The balcony (1.7 m) runs along the playroom's east wall, the last 3 m of it, with its ramp in the 2 m before. X is east, Z is north, in metres; yaw is degrees clockwise from north; furniture 'y' is height above the room floor. Rooms marked outdoor have no ceiling and a garden or paved floor.",
